---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Support Hekara"
  description="Sponsor the Hekara project or hire for custom solutions, integrations, and compliance help."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Support Hekara Development</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Hekara is free, open-source scheduling software for home health agencies. Sponsorship keeps it maintained, tested, and documented while enabling contributors to be paid for their work.
      </p>

      <!-- Sponsor Card -->
      <div class="card mt-4">
        <h2>Sponsor with Any Amount</h2>
        <p>
          Pay by UPI, card, or net banking through Razorpay. Choose the amount that fits your budget. Sponsorship is voluntary and does not buy a product or guarantee (see the <a href="/Hekara/terms">terms</a>).
        </p>
        <a href="https://rzp.io/rzp/G5kLjzP" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Sponsor with Razorpay
        </a>
        <p class="text-muted mt-2">Payments are processed by Razorpay. Your card and bank details never reach this site or the project.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-4">Who Should Sponsor?</h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 mt-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>If you're an agency or clinic running Hekara</h3>
          <p><strong>Fair way to give back:</strong> Sponsor monthly (even a small amount) or hire for support, setup, hosting, and training. It costs far less than per-seat SaaS software.</p>
          <p class="text-muted">Every sponsorship directly funds maintenance, security updates, and community support.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>If you're a company building a product on Hekara</h3>
          <p><strong>Fair way to give back:</strong> Sponsor at a level matching the value you receive, fund a specific feature, or inquire about commercial licenses.</p>
          <p class="text-muted">Your users benefit from a secure, maintained foundation. Help keep it that way.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>If you're a developer</h3>
          <p><strong>Fair way to contribute:</strong> Fix a bug, send a pull request, or take a paid bounty for your work.</p>
          <p class="text-muted">Contributions earn bounties shared from sponsorship funds. See <a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/docs/FUNDING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/FUNDING.md</a> for details.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Individual or student?</h3>
          <p><strong>How to help:</strong> Star the GitHub repo, share with others, or sponsor what you can afford.</p>
          <p class="text-muted">Every contribution matters. Even $1 helps show that people care about this project.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-4">What Your Sponsorship Funds</h2>
      
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Maintainer time:</strong> Fixing bugs, reviewing contributions, keeping the project secure, documented, and up-to-date.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contributors:</strong> A share of sponsorship funds as bounties for merged work. The rules are public in <a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/docs/FUNDING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/FUNDING.md</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Infrastructure:</strong> Hosting for demos, testing, an independent security audit, and long-term project sustainability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Community:</strong> Documentation, examples, and helping other agencies implement Hekara successfully.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-4">Other Ways to Help</h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 mt-3">
        <div class="card card-compact text-center">
          <h3>⭐ Star & Share</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Star the <a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repo</a> and share with other agencies and developers.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-compact text-center">
          <h3>Contribute Code</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Pick a <a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/labels/good%20first%20issue" target="_blank" rel="noopener">good first issue</a> or improve the documentation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-compact text-center">
          <h3>Provide Feedback</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Use Hekara, report bugs, suggest features, and share your story.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-4">Paid Support & Custom Work</h2>
      
      <p>
        Organizations can engage the maintainer for:
      </p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Installation & hosting</strong> – Setup on Cloudflare, AWS, Node.js, or on-premises</li>
        <li><strong>Integrations</strong> – EHR, payroll, clearinghouses, SSO (SAML, OIDC)</li>
        <li><strong>Custom features</strong> – Tailored workflows for your agency</li>
        <li><strong>Migrations</strong> – Move from your current system without data loss</li>
        <li><strong>Training</strong> – Get your team up to speed</li>
        <li><strong>Compliance & GRC</strong> – HIPAA, SOC 2, ISO 27001 readiness</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Scope and fees are agreed in writing before work starts and invoiced in INR or USD. See <a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/COMMERCIAL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COMMERCIAL.md</a> for details.
      </p>

      <div class="card mt-4">
        <h3>Interested in Custom Solutions?</h3>
        <p>Contact the maintainer for a conversation about your needs.</p>
        <a href="/Hekara/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-4">Important Notes</h2>
      
      <blockquote>
        <strong>Sponsorship is voluntary.</strong> It does not buy a product, guarantee, or support contract. Hekara is free under the AGPL-3.0 license. Paid support and custom work are separate offerings.
      </blockquote>

      <blockquote>
        <strong>Hekara is not certified.</strong> No software can hold HIPAA, SOC 2, or ISO 27001 certifications on its own. Hekara provides technical safeguards (encryption, audit logs, access control). Compliance is the responsibility of the organization deploying and operating it.
      </blockquote>

      <blockquote>
        <strong>Your privacy is protected.</strong> Sponsorship is not marketing. No email is shared, no lists are built. You receive a thank-you and that's it.
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="mt-4">Transparency</h2>
      
      <p>
        Hekara is maintained by <strong>Nampalli Srinivas</strong>, an individual developer and GRC specialist in India. All decisions are open, all code is public, and all funding sources are disclosed.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/docs/FUNDING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Funding guide</a> (how sponsorship is used)</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/COMMERCIAL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Commercial offerings</a> (what's available)</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Security guide</a> (safeguards and responsibility)</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Srinivas26k/Hekara/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AGPL-3.0 License</a> (what you can do with Hekara)</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- Final CTA -->
      <div class="card mt-4" >
        <h2>Ready to Support Hekara?</h2>
        <p>Your sponsorship—no matter the amount—helps keep this project alive and improving.</p>
        <a href="https://rzp.io/rzp/G5kLjzP" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Sponsor Now
        </a>
        <p class="text-muted mt-2">Or explore <a href="/Hekara/contact">custom solutions and paid support</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
